{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-27T05:24:27.089Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"6a627c6a9d6772d54597ee42","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"argv"},"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"create","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/id","value":"pm-x17o8l"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/title","value":"A wrong-typed member in schema/statuses.json or schema/types.json (a numeric description, a numeric alias) throws in its normalizer and resets every setting to its default"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/description","value":"Found 2026-11-27 while fixing pm-x9r2h3. loadRuntimeSchemaFromOptionalFiles now skips status and field entries that are not objects and type entries without a string name, but the status and type normalizers still call trim on members they assume are strings: a status with description 5, or a type with description 5 or aliases [5], throws inside the settings read, which then fails its merge (settings_read_merge_failed) and every setting falls back to its default. The field normalizer was hardened in pm-x9r2h3 (non-string description is ignored and reported); statuses and types need the same treatment, plus a validate report of what was ignored. Reproduced on the built CLI by calling normalizeRuntimeSchemaSettings with statuses [{ id: 'x', description: 5 }] and normalizeItemTypeDefinitions with [{ name: 'X', description: 5 }]. Duplicate check: searched statuses types normalizer description crash settings_read_merge_failed; no open item covers it."},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/type","value":"Issue"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/status","value":"open"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/priority","value":2},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/tags","value":["area:schema","robustness","settings","validation"]},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/created_at","value":"2026-11-27T05:24:27.089Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-27T05:24:27.089Z"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/author","value":"harness:claude-code"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/estimated_minutes","value":120},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/acceptance_criteria","value":"A status or type schema file entry with any wrong-typed member no longer fails the settings read; the member is ignored and the rest of the entry and of the settings load; pm validate or pm health names each ignored member with its file and position; A spec seeds wrong-typed members for every string and list member of a status and a type definition, with a negative control on the current release"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/parent","value":"pm-8jdc"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/risk","value":"medium"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/confidence","value":"high"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/expected_result","value":"One malformed member in a schema file cannot reset every setting"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/actual_result","value":"settings_read_merge_failed and defaults for the whole tracker"},{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/dependencies","value":[{"id":"pm-x9r2h3","kind":"discovered_from","created_at":"2026-11-27T05:24:27.089Z","author":"harness:claude-code","source_kind":"cli:create:dep","author_source":"detected"}]}],"before_hash":"3cc22dff72be7b14824654a7a64ea62b04799939b2fee54c1b5f52ca60bf6df0","after_hash":"0335e1c46bc683ed96d2184e1cd5080b3e857e5b2b95c4a176f02434fc84613d","item_hash_version":3,"message":"","context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"c1396e912e752204590d9a6dc7110f01d1a229cb46a75ca87444e0ade9f2e30f"}
