{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-28T14:45:20.590Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"39f0409326ff3a93bdf4de17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":{"value":"implementer","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-928ng6","lineage:pm-928ng6","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"topic":{"value":"pm-928ng6","source":"inferred","confidence":"medium","rule_version":"v2","evidence":["claim:pm-928ng6","lineage:pm-928ng6","lineage:pm-u9d0","lineage:pm-doxj"]},"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/1","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-28T14:45:20.589Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 1 (2026-11-28), two P2s and a P3, valid and fixed. (1) In a schema file, required: 'false' on a type option turned into a requirement through Boolean(). inspectItemTypeDefinition now takes its source (extension | schema_file): for a schema file a non-boolean switch is ignored and reported, while an extension registration keeps its earlier Boolean reading. (2) required_create_fields: [5] became an explicit empty override and cleared the built-in create requirements of an overridden type. A non-empty list with no usable entry now reads as absent, while [] stays an explicit override. (3) A blank option key or policy option target passed inspection and was then dropped silently by the normalizer. Both are now dropped and reported in the inspection."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-28T14:45:20.590Z"}],"before_hash":"7add7c69d4fe7e71b5980ba2f531742920058230eb9d4c4a1073121d769f3b53","after_hash":"aa19d5cb680dd9fd3f6db8158838c24eab94465105c690647107fa5e0d02f234","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"dd8c70bc1908c7d3f5c118605a6da430db26d5d2333676008fd6d807cec93778"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-28T15:35:36.030Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"39f0409326ff3a93bdf4de17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/2","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-28T15:35:36.029Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 2, 2026-11-28, P2, valid: required_create_fields [5, ' '] kept the blank string, which the normalizer then emptied into an explicit [] override, so strict create lost the built-in Task requirements. Blank strings are now unusable like wrong-typed entries, each is reported as is blank, and a non-empty list with no usable entry reads as absent. The spec checks the registry keeps the built-in Task requirements, and that an intentional [] stays an override."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-28T15:35:36.030Z"}],"before_hash":"aa19d5cb680dd9fd3f6db8158838c24eab94465105c690647107fa5e0d02f234","after_hash":"af4fedde475e9df924b5c2bfd05cc06be74ff17527c432374956808ff699a42e","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"36f5cdb6916545e4001cf1f8b8f2d63a165b3bfccef2dcdcaea0bccb7a16f4e6"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-28T15:50:43.938Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"39f0409326ff3a93bdf4de17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-28T15:50:43.938Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Greptile P1 and CodeRabbit Major on PR #1795, 2026-11-28: blank entries in required_create_fields were the same finding as Codex round 2 and were already fixed. A further CodeRabbit Major, valid: options [null] or command_option_policies [7] read as an explicit empty list, which overrode the options and policies a type already had. readRecordList now applies the string-list rule: a non-empty list with no usable record reads as absent, while an explicit [] stays an override."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-28T15:50:43.938Z"}],"before_hash":"af4fedde475e9df924b5c2bfd05cc06be74ff17527c432374956808ff699a42e","after_hash":"5bfc6a87cac39e35dea3448a1ada4ffcd4c78bce202de5c909efd799fb947e72","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"d8f07aec0bd7d22d65d3a307d7654854c067e1ab0595dd66326ec2612c0485b1"}
{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-11-28T16:04:41.726Z","author":"harness:claude-code","author_source":"detected","agent_harness":"claude-code","agent_model":"claude-opus-5-5","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"39f0409326ff3a93bdf4de17","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"claude-opus-5-5","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"environment"},"role":null,"topic":null,"version":{"value":"2.1.332","source":"probe"}},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/4","value":{"created_at":"2026-11-28T16:04:41.725Z","author":"harness:claude-code","text":"Codex review round 3, 2026-11-28. One fixed: an option whose supplied values allowlist has no usable value (values [null, ' ']) became an unrestricted option through the ?? [] default. It is now dropped and reported, for schema files and registrations alike. One declined, with reason: a schema/types.json entry replacing an inline settings definition of the same name is the existing replace-by-name semantics (normalizeItemTypeDefinitions dedupes, and the later entry wins). It applies equally to well-typed entries, and this change does not introduce it. Before the change, the same file made the read fall back to defaults, which lost the inline definition too."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-11-28T16:04:41.726Z"}],"before_hash":"5bfc6a87cac39e35dea3448a1ada4ffcd4c78bce202de5c909efd799fb947e72","after_hash":"d17be5a9a028027272154f871a84c170e24f99e53faddbed3f741847fc0cccb2","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"version":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"claude_session_file","rule_version":"v1"}}},"event_class":"substantive","record_hash_version":1,"record_hash":"93bed53328eeaf94977f140ff08a90a105391e7ee96037134687b5ca82582cf4"}
